# Copy, Claims & Content

## Privacy Claims Are Load-Bearing

`/privacy` is the public privacy URL (`public/privacy.html`; `/privacy.html` 301s). That `.html` path is still the App Store listing URL. Site copy is a compliance surface, not just marketing. Every claim must be true of the shipping app:

- Free — no ads, no account, no subscription, no credits (all IAP removed from sale as of 4.0)
- By default, notes never leave the device except to sync through the user's own private iCloud
- Search, answers, and understanding run on-device with Apple Intelligence
- Every context signal has an off switch
- App Privacy discloses optional Pro Mode BYOK (Other User Content + Photos for App Functionality, not tracking)

**Never add a claim the app doesn't back.** If a feature changes what leaves the device, `/privacy`, the `#privacy` section, and `#pro-mode` on the landing page change in the same commit.

One distinction to keep straight: **Pro Mode** (bring-your-own-key web search — OpenAI or Anthropic — opt-in, off by default) is the single path that sends note text and photos off-device, and only on an explicit user action. It is not the same as capture-time understanding, which is always on-device. Don't blur the two in copy. Lead with provider choice and user-controlled costs when highlighting BYOK.

## Positioning

- "A notebook, not a database" — no folders, no tags to manage, no sorting
- Retrieval by memory: "coffee shop notes," "rainy day ideas," "notes from Traverse City"
- Calm and emptiness are the point. Don't write dashboard or productivity-tool copy.

## Platform Copy — Check Before Propagating

Current copy covers iPhone and Mac. Keep Universal Purchase language consistent when editing hero, `.fine` line, `#privacy`, meta descriptions, and og tags.

## Adding a Blog Post

Create `public/blog/<slug>.html`, then three updates or the post is orphaned:

1. A `<li>` in `public/blog/index.html` → `.postlist`, with `.date`, `.title` link, and `.excerpt`
2. A `<url>` entry in `public/sitemap.xml` with the **final** canonical `<loc>` (no `.html`), `<lastmod>`, and `<priority>0.7</priority>`
3. The post's own `<title>`, `meta description`, and og tags

Link to posts **extensionless**: `/blog/<slug>`, never `/blog/<slug>.html`.

## Per-Page Requirements

- `<title>` suffixed `— Musing`, plus a real `meta name="description"`
- `rel="canonical"` on the final public URL (homepage `/` and blog index `/blog/` with trailing slash; posts `/blog/<slug>` and privacy `/privacy` without)
- Open Graph: `og:type`, `og:site_name`, `og:title`, `og:description`, `og:image` (absolute `https://musingnotes.app/og-card.png`), `og:url` matching the canonical
- Twitter: `twitter:card`, `twitter:title`, `twitter:description`, `twitter:image`
- Icons: `/favicon.ico` and `/apple-touch-icon.png` (180×180) — not the 1024 `icon.png` master
- Root-relative `/styles.css` and `/theme.js`
- `<html lang="en" data-theme="foolscap">`
- Decorative glyphs (`⚙`, `◉`, `︿`, dot spans) get `aria-hidden="true"`; interactive swatches keep `aria-pressed` and `role="tablist"` on the picker
